\ 0f assembler in 0f - 1f
\ features are the same as shell/python version
\ one line
\ %macro ... code ...  %% 
\ macros cannot be defined in macros
\ :label code
\ labels are compile-time only
\ inserts a "call" instruction

\ --- data structures ---
\ input buffer - 24kb
\ self explanatory. contains the input program text. persistent

\ output buffer - 24kb
\ these are small because the programs written in 0f should not be large
\ 1f really should only be used to write hello world and 1f.0f 

\ dict - 24kb
\ dict is NOT a linked list. static size
\ dict entry consists of string length (byte), name address (word), code address (word). stored as offset into input buffer or output buffer.
\ name addresses are stored as offsets into the input buffer
\ one byte before each name address will be '%' or ':'. this will determine the execution behavuour

\ words for compiling empty space into the program
\ how to loop without loops

%4z $0000 $0000 %%
%16z 4z 4z 4z 4z %%
%64z 16z 16z 16z 16z %%
%256z 64z 64z 64z %%

\ one kilozero
%1kz 256z 256z 256z 256z %%
%4kz 1kz 1kz 1kz 1kz %%
%24kz 4kz 4kz 4kz 4kz 4kz 4kz %%

\ $$ is a placeholder for source location. i think this works

:dict push $$ ; 24kz
:inb  push $$ ; 24kz
:outb push $$ ; 24kz
\ output will need to be dynamically allocated in the actual program


\ != = should only consume TOS and set the conditional flag maybe?
\ +; exit if condition flag is true
\ -; exit if condition flag is false
\ _ before a word indicates it deals in bytes rather than words

\ assumes b is inb

\ as long as you're seeing a space, iterate
:wl _b@+ push $20 != +; wl ;
:word b wl b over - swap ;

\ searches dict and returns dict entry
:search ;

\ takes a word, performs the corresponding action
\ def? and parse might be mutually recursive. figure it out? 
:parse  dup _@ lit? +; macro? +; label? +; def? +; err ;

\ first character
:macro? push $25 != -; drop push $01 + swap dict _!+ dict !+ inb dict !+ ;

:label? push $3b != -; drop push $01 + swap dict _!+ dict !+ outb dict !+ ;

\ push the length, then the pointer (?) into the input buffer for the name +1 byte (for S= purposes)
\ then ush the 

